IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei5-sickness-pregnancy`

-- Tests of ei5-sickness-pregnancy (Act ss 152.03 and 152.04). Expected values are written by hand from the text
-- beside each assertion; the dates are worked out on a calendar (2026-10-24 is a Saturday, so 2026-10-18 is a Sunday).

§ `152.03(1), (1.1) and (4) entitlement`

-- arguments: prescribed illness, unable to work for that reason, ceased to work because of it, would otherwise be
-- working, benefits payable under any of ss 152.05 to 152.062
#ASSERT `s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- would not be working anyway and no (1.1) benefits: not entitled
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- did not cease to work because of the illness and no (1.1) benefits: not entitled
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (1.1): benefits payable under s 152.05, so entitled although they did not cease to work and would not be working
#ASSERT `s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- not a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- not unable to work: "while unable to work", even under (1.1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- (4): arguments: benefits payable under 152.05 to 152.062 (the (1.1) person), would be deemed not working but for the illness
#ASSERT `s 152.03(4) a self-employed person is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE
-- a person referred to in (1.1) is excluded from (4)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(4) a self-employed person is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(4) a self-employed person is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03(4) a self-employed person is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE)

-- both together: all six arguments
#ASSERT `s 152.03 entitled to benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- (4) takes it away: but for the illness the person would be deemed not to be working
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.03 entitled to benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- the (1.1) person is not caught by (4)
#ASSERT `s 152.03 entitled to benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `The reductions repeated by ss 152.03 to 152.062`

-- benefits of 500 a week, allowances payable under a provincial law, reduction prescribed 120: 380
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(2), 152.04(3), 152.05(11), 152.06(9), 152.061(11) and 152.062(9) benefits after the reduction prescribed for benefits payable under a provincial law` 500 TRUE 120 EQUALS 380
-- "reduced or eliminated": a reduction as large as the benefit eliminates it; it does not go below zero
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(2), 152.04(3), 152.05(11), 152.06(9), 152.061(11) and 152.062(9) benefits after the reduction prescribed for benefits payable under a provincial law` 500 TRUE 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(2), 152.04(3), 152.05(11), 152.06(9), 152.061(11) and 152.062(9) benefits after the reduction prescribed for benefits payable under a provincial law` 500 TRUE 600 EQUALS 0
-- nothing payable under a provincial law: no reduction
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(2), 152.04(3), 152.05(11), 152.06(9), 152.061(11) and 152.062(9) benefits after the reduction prescribed for benefits payable under a provincial law` 500 FALSE 120 EQUALS 500

-- deduction of allowances under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(3) and 152.04(4) benefits after the deduction of allowances payable under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced` 500 120 EQUALS 380
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(3) and 152.04(4) benefits after the deduction of allowances payable under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced` 500 0 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(3) and 152.04(4) benefits after the deduction of allowances payable under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced` 500 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `ss 152.03(3) and 152.04(4) benefits after the deduction of allowances payable under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced` 500 600 EQUALS 0

§ `152.04(1) and (2) pregnancy`

#ASSERT `s 152.04(1) benefits are payable because of pregnancy` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 152.04(1) benefits are payable because of pregnancy` FALSE)

-- Confinement expected on Wednesday 10 June 2026; the Sunday of that week is 7 June 2026.
-- Twelve weeks before is 15 March 2026. Seventeen weeks after 7 June is Sunday 4 October, so the period ends
-- on Saturday 10 October 2026.
-- not yet occurred: the period the expected date gives
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 10) NOTHING EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- confinement on the expected day
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- confinement early (Wednesday 20 May, week of Sunday 17 May): the earlier week is 15 March (12 weeks before the
-- expected week), the later is the expected week: the same period
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 5 20)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- confinement very early (Wednesday 25 February, week of Sunday 22 February): earlier than 15 March, so it begins
-- on 22 February; the later week is still 7 June, so it ends 10 October
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 2 25)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 2 22), (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- confinement late (Wednesday 1 July, week of Sunday 28 June): begins 15 March; 17 weeks after 28 June is Sunday
-- 25 October, so it ends Saturday 31 October
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 31)
-- the week boundary: expected on Saturday 13 June is still the week of 7 June ...
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 13) NOTHING EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- ... and on Sunday 14 June it is the next week: a week later at both ends
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 14) NOTHING EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 22), (YMD 2026 10 17)
-- expected on a Sunday, 7 June: that week
#ASSERT `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` (YMD 2026 6 7) NOTHING EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)

-- (3.1) the week that immediately precedes the period is deemed included: 8 March to 10 October
#ASSERT `s 152.04(3.1) the period, for serving the waiting period, with the week that immediately precedes it` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 8), (YMD 2026 10 10)

§ `152.04(5) and (6) a hospitalized child`

-- Confinement on 10 June 2026 (week of 7 June); 52 weeks after that week is Sunday 6 June 2027, so the
-- extended period may end no later than Saturday 12 June 2027.
`the base pregnancy period` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- no weeks in hospital: unchanged
#ASSERT `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` `the base pregnancy period` (YMD 2026 6 10) 0 EQUALS `the base pregnancy period`
-- 3 weeks: 10 October + 21 days = 31 October
#ASSERT `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` `the base pregnancy period` (YMD 2026 6 10) 3 EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2026 10 31)
-- 34 weeks: 10 October + 238 days = 5 June 2027, a week short of the limit
#ASSERT `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` `the base pregnancy period` (YMD 2026 6 10) 34 EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2027 6 5)
-- 35 weeks: 10 October + 245 days = 12 June 2027, exactly the limit
#ASSERT `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` `the base pregnancy period` (YMD 2026 6 10) 35 EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2027 6 12)
-- 36 weeks would reach 19 June 2027: held at the limit
#ASSERT `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` `the base pregnancy period` (YMD 2026 6 10) 36 EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2027 6 12)
#ASSERT `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` `the base pregnancy period` (YMD 2026 6 10) 40 EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 15), (YMD 2027 6 12)
